.TH sjinfo "1" "Slurm Commands" "May 2026" "Slurm Commands"

.SH "NAME"
sjinfo \- Display Slurm job resource consumption and abnormal event information

.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBsjinfo\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR...]

.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
\fBsjinfo\fR displays resource consumption information, abnormal event
information, application type information, job summary information, and
user-defined messages collected for Slurm jobs.
.PP
The command reads job monitoring data from the configured accounting backend.
Most queries can be restricted by job id, step id, time range, user, event type,
or output field list.

.SH "OPTIONS"

.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-all\fR
Equivalent to specifying \fB\-l\fR, \fB\-A\fR, and \fB\-O\fR simultaneously.
.IP

.TP
\fB\-A\fR, \fB\-\-abnormal\fR
Display information about abnormal events during job execution.
.IP

.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-desc\fR
Output data in reverse order.
.IP

.TP
\fB\-D\fR, \fB\-\-display\fR
Print brief job information. CPU Efficiency and MEM Efficiency are normalized
values.
.IP

.TP
\fB\-e\fR, \fB\-\-event\fR=<\fIfield_list\fR>
Print the selected abnormal event types. This option must be used with
\fB\-A\fR or \fB\-O\fR.
.RS
.TP
\fBCPUUSA\fR
CPU Utilization State Anomaly.
.TP
\fBPidSA\fR
Process State Anomaly.
.TP
\fBNodeSA\fR
Node State Anomaly.
.TP
\fBGPUUSA\fR
GPU Utilization State Anomaly.
.RE
.IP

.TP
\fB\-E\fR, \fB\-\-end\fR=<\fItime\fR>
Set the end time of the abnormal event query.
.IP

.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Display help information and exit.
.IP

.TP
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-\-jobs\fR=<\fIjobid\fR[,\fIjobid\fR...]>
Specify the job ID or comma-separated job ID list to query.
.IP

.TP
\fB\-J\fR, \fB\-\-job\-summary\fR
Display job step data aggregated to job level.
.IP

.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-load\fR
Display load and resource consumption information during job run time.
.IP

.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR=<\fIfield_list\fR>
Print the selected comma-separated list of fields.
.IP
Supported field names include:
.RS
.PP
\fBJobID\fR, \fBStepID\fR, \fBStepCPU\fR, \fBStepAVECPU\fR,
\fBStepMEM\fR, \fBStepVMEM\fR, \fBStepPages\fR, \fBMaxStepCPU\fR,
\fBMinStepCPU\fR, \fBMaxStepMEM\fR, \fBMinStepMEM\fR,
\fBMaxStepVMEM\fR, \fBMinStepVMEM\fR, \fBStepGPU(DCU)\fR,
\fBStepGPU(DCU)MEM\fR, \fBMaxStepGPU(DCU)\fR, \fBMinStepGPU(DCU)\fR,
\fBMaxStepGPU(DCU)MEM\fR, \fBMinStepGPU(DCU)MEM\fR,
\fBCPUthreshold\fR, \fBGRESthreshold\fR, \fBStart\fR, \fBEnd\fR,
\fBType\fR, \fBLast_start\fR, \fBLast_end\fR,
\fBCPU_Abnormal_CNT\fR, \fBPROC_Abnormal_CNT\fR,
\fBNODE_Abnormal_CNT\fR, \fBGPU_Abnormal_CNT\fR,
\fBTotalCPU\fR, \fBTotalMEM\fR, \fBTotalVMEM\fR, \fBTotalPages\fR,
\fBMaxCPU\fR, \fBMinCPU\fR, \fBMaxMEM\fR, \fBMinMEM\fR,
\fBMaxVMEM\fR, \fBMinVMEM\fR, \fBTotalGPU(DCU)\fR,
\fBTotalGPU(DCU)MEM\fR, \fBMaxGPU(DCU)\fR, \fBMinGPU(DCU)\fR,
\fBMaxGPU(DCU)MEM\fR, and \fBMinGPU(DCU)MEM\fR.
.RE
.IP

.TP
\fB\-O\fR, \fB\-\-overall\fR
Display overall abnormal event information.
.IP

.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-steps\fR=<\fIstep\fR[,\fIstep\fR...]>
Specify job steps to query. The special step names \fBbatch\fR and
\fBextern\fR are supported.
.IP

.TP
\fB\-S\fR, \fB\-\-start\fR=<\fItime\fR>
Set the start time of the abnormal event query, for example
\fB2024\-05\-07T08:00:00\fR.
.IP

.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-apptype\fR[=<\fIjob|step\fR>]
Display application type information for the job. Use \fBstep\fR to display
application type information at the job step level. The default is job level.
.IP

.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print the sjinfo version and exit.
.IP

.TP
\fB\-m\fR
Convert KB values to MB. The default unit is KB.
.IP

.TP
\fB\-g\fR
Convert KB values to GB. The default unit is KB.
.IP

.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-query\fR
Query user-defined messages. The query output can include job ID, user name,
step ID, user UID, message content, send node, and post time. If \fBJSNS\fR
appears in the job step column, the job step was not specified when the message
was written.
.IP

.TP
\fB\-u\fR, \fB\-\-user\fR=<\fIuser\fR>
Query data for the specified user.
.IP

.SH "FIELD DESCRIPTIONS"

.SS "Resource Consumption Fields"
.TP
\fBJobID\fR
Job ID.
.TP
\fBStepID\fR
Job step ID.
.TP
\fBStepCPU\fR
CPU utilization within the job step anomaly detection interval.
.TP
\fBStepAVECPU\fR
Average CPU utilization of the job step.
.TP
\fBStepMEM\fR
Real-time memory usage of the job step.
.TP
\fBStepVMEM\fR
Real-time virtual memory usage of the job step.
.TP
\fBStepPages\fR
Job step page fault count during the current job step running cycle.
.TP
\fBMaxStepCPU\fR, \fBMinStepCPU\fR
Maximum and minimum CPU utilization during the current job step running cycle.
.TP
\fBMaxStepMEM\fR, \fBMinStepMEM\fR
Maximum and minimum memory usage during the current job step running cycle.
.TP
\fBMaxStepVMEM\fR, \fBMinStepVMEM\fR
Maximum and minimum virtual memory usage during the current job step running
cycle.
.TP
\fBStepGPU(DCU)\fR, \fBStepGPU(DCU)MEM\fR
GPU/DCU utilization and GPU/DCU memory usage for the job step.

.SS "Job Summary Fields"
.TP
\fBTotalCPU\fR, \fBTotalMEM\fR, \fBTotalVMEM\fR, \fBTotalPages\fR
Total CPU utilization, memory usage, virtual memory usage, and page faults
across all job steps.
.TP
\fBMaxCPU\fR, \fBMinCPU\fR
Maximum and minimum CPU utilization across all job steps.
.TP
\fBMaxMEM\fR, \fBMinMEM\fR
Maximum and minimum memory usage across all job steps.
.TP
\fBMaxVMEM\fR, \fBMinVMEM\fR
Maximum and minimum virtual memory usage across all job steps.
.TP
\fBTotalGPU(DCU)\fR, \fBTotalGPU(DCU)MEM\fR
Total GPU/DCU utilization and memory usage across all job steps.
.TP
\fBMaxGPU(DCU)\fR, \fBMinGPU(DCU)\fR
Maximum and minimum GPU/DCU utilization across all job steps.
.TP
\fBMaxGPU(DCU)MEM\fR, \fBMinGPU(DCU)MEM\fR
Maximum and minimum GPU/DCU memory usage across all job steps.

.SS "Abnormal Event Fields"
.TP
\fBCPUthreshold\fR
CPU utilization threshold for the job.
.TP
\fBGRESthreshold\fR
GPU utilization threshold for the job.
.TP
\fBStart\fR
Start time of the abnormal event.
.TP
\fBEnd\fR
End time of the abnormal event.
.TP
\fBType\fR
Type of abnormal event.

.SS "Abnormal Event Overall Fields"
.TP
\fBLast_start\fR
Start time of the most recent anomaly.
.TP
\fBLast_end\fR
End time of the most recent anomaly.
.TP
\fBCPU_Abnormal_CNT\fR
Total number of CPU abnormal events.
.TP
\fBPROC_Abnormal_CNT\fR
Total number of process abnormal events.
.TP
\fBNODE_Abnormal_CNT\fR
Total number of node abnormal events.
.TP
\fBGPU_Abnormal_CNT\fR
Total number of GPU abnormal events.

.SH "EXAMPLES"
.TP
\fBsjinfo \-j 135617 \-a\fR
Display load, abnormal event, and overall abnormal event information for job
135617.
.TP
\fBsjinfo \-j 135617 \-A \-e GPUUSA\fR
Display GPU abnormal events for job 135617.
.TP
\fBsjinfo \-j 135617 \-s extern \-A\fR
Display abnormal events for the extern step of job 135617.
.TP
\fBsjinfo \-j 135617 \-J\fR
Display job-level aggregated resource consumption information.

.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBsacct\fR(1), \fBsstat\fR(1), \fBsrun\fR(1)
